import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — JOINT_SHAPES: the enumeration's correlated corner, reached","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — \`JOINT_SHAPES\`: the enumeration's correlated corner, reached","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-19T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/joint-shape-schemata.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/joint-shape-schemata.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/joint-shape-schemata.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-joint-shapes-the-enumeration-s-correlated-corner-reached" tabindex="-1">Retro — <code>JOINT_SHAPES</code>: the enumeration&#39;s correlated corner, reached <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-joint-shapes-the-enumeration-s-correlated-corner-reached" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — JOINT_SHAPES: the enumeration&#39;s correlated corner, reached”">​</a></h1><p><strong>Follows</strong>: <code>binding-env-cap.md</code> (its named residual — &quot;the binding banks have no conv-weight-shaped inhabitants; the named fix remains a corner-reaching enumeration vocabulary&quot;) and <code>fixpoint-api-and-conv-sweep.md</code> (the 60-anchor starvation account). <strong>Commit</strong>: <code>819beeb</code> (the machinery + data), this commit (retro + GOALS).</p><h2 id="the-gap-precisely" tabindex="-1">The gap, precisely <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-gap-precisely" aria-label="Permalink to “The gap, precisely”">​</a></h2><p><code>_binding_envs</code> binds every leaf metavariable <strong>independently</strong> — <code>_viewed_bindings</code> diag-products per-metavar banks, <code>_pull_bases</code> does the same for the free dimension. A guard whose accepted region is a <em>relation across operands</em> is unreachable no matter the window:</p><ul><li><code>conv2d</code>&#39;s <code>x[1] == W[1]·groups</code> <em>and</em> <code>b == (W[0],)</code> — three relations over three metavars;</li><li><code>batch_norm</code>&#39;s four stat vectors all <code>(x[1],)</code> — five relations;</li><li>the pointwise sibling&#39;s <code>(1, C, 1, 1)</code> channel view — a rank-4 singleton the pad/derived transforms never mint (pad insertions only <em>prepend</em> axes, never mask a same-rank one).</li></ul><p>Measured on the conv+BN composite: <code>0 accepted / 2000 declined / 2360 envs</code> — the corner was not <em>late</em> in the order, it was outside the domain.</p><h2 id="the-fix-—-data-not-special-casing" tabindex="-1">The fix — data, not special-casing <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-fix-—-data-not-special-casing" aria-label="Permalink to “The fix — data, not special-casing”">​</a></h2><p><code>lawdata.JOINT_SHAPES</code> keys <code>(op, arity)</code> → concrete correlated operand-shape rows (<code>(x, W, b)</code> = <code>(2,4,8,8),(6,4,3,3),(6,)</code> &amp;c.). The engine is three generic pieces:</p><ol><li><strong><code>_joint_plan</code></strong> — finds tabulated nodes with metavar args (<code>_joint_nodes</code>, a <code>_view_nodes</code>-style walk keyed <code>(op, arity)</code>), builds each node&#39;s row options (positional binding, <code>Var</code>s), and merges the product under Var <em>agreement</em> — two nodes pinning the same metavar must draw identically or the combo dies. Coverage = union of bound names.</li><li><strong>Coverage replaces the independent draw</strong> — a covered metavar leaves both <code>viewed</code> and <code>free</code>; the joint combos ride the <code>_viewed_bindings</code> product as dimension 0, so the coherent corner <em>leads</em> the enumeration. Joint-free patterns enumerate byte-identically (the dim degenerates to <code>[{}]</code>).</li><li><strong><code>JOINT_VIEW_SHAPES</code></strong> — the <code>(1,C,1,1)</code> channel-view corner, appended via the existing <code>extra_viewed</code> channel (the <code>CHAIN_VIEWED_SHAPES</code> scoping idiom) for joint patterns only.</li></ol><p>Plus one attr-kind correction the sweep <em>measured</em>: conv2d&#39;s <code>stride</code> drew <code>0</code> from the generic <code>int</code> domain and every accepted anchor site died <code>non-positive stride</code> — <code>(&quot;conv2d&quot;,&quot;stride&quot;)</code> is now a <code>pos-int</code> override; <code>dilation</code>/<code>groups</code> are positive by name default (<code>as_strided</code> keeps <code>stride: int</code> — its 0 is legal).</p><h2 id="the-measured-verdict" tabindex="-1">The measured verdict <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-measured-verdict" aria-label="Permalink to “The measured verdict”">​</a></h2><p><code>lab/probes/conv_fold_premise_pay_probe.py</code>, gauntlet leg:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>stage</th><th>before (<code>0721cec</code>)</th><th>after</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>truth (synth region)</td><td><code>0 accepted / 2000 declined / 2360 envs</code></td><td><strong><code>105 accepted / 105 equal / 0 ne / 0 rerr</code> in 360 envs — PASS</strong></td></tr><tr><td>derivable</td><td>False → (premise-anchored) True</td><td><code>True(premise-anchored)</code> — unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>novelty</td><td>— (unreached)</td><td>pass (<code>new</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>typed-pay</td><td>— (unreached)</td><td><strong>pass: fires=1 typed=1 ill=0 paid=1</strong></td></tr><tr><td>closure</td><td>— (unreached)</td><td><strong>FAIL: <code>enode=6.00x</code> vs the cap</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Anchors (<code>_guarded_evals</code> @ 360, no escalation): all six measured variants now read <code>accepted&gt;0, equal==accepted, unequal=0</code> — <code>scale_sp</code> 7/7, <code>scale</code> 10/10, <code>shift_sp</code> 8/8, <code>scale_spdg</code> 6/6 (the groups=2 corner also accepts: <code>x[1]==W[1]·2</code>), <code>scale_nobias</code> 14/14, <code>shift_sub_sp</code> 8/8. <code>batch_norm_expand</code> keeps its corner — the joint rows satisfy the stat-vector contract it already swept.</p><p>The truth-side blocker is <strong>closed</strong>. The composite&#39;s refusal moved to <strong>stage 7 (closure)</strong>: <code>enode=6.00x</code> — the fold&#39;s RHS expansion grows the one-term graph past the closure bound. That is a <em>different</em> gate (cost-side, already named in <code>premise-anchored-derivability.md</code>), not a truth question.</p><h2 id="what-stays-open" tabindex="-1">What stays open <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-open" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays open”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Closure bound vs expansion rules</strong>: <code>enode=6.00x</code> is the composite&#39;s honest expansion ratio on the one-case corpus — whether <code>_CLOSURE_LIMIT</code> should distinguish &quot;fold mints a big RHS member&quot; from runaway blow-up is the next named policy question.</li><li><strong><code>matmul</code>/<code>linear</code>/<code>sdpa</code> joint rows</strong>: deliberately left out — their sweeps measure today, and a covered metavar&#39;s domain <em>is</em> the row set, so an unneeded entry shrinks a working domain (the <code>CONST_DOMAIN</code> discipline). Add a row only when a starvation is measured.</li><li><strong>Witness-driven sites</strong>: the retro&#39;s alternative route (drive the sweep from real fold sites) is now unnecessary for this corner — the enumeration reaches it — but remains the honest answer for a corner no row vocabulary can name (data-dependent shapes).</li></ul><h2 id="gate-account" tabindex="-1">Gate account <a class="header-anchor" href="#gate-account" aria-label="Permalink to “Gate account”">​</a></h2><p><code>tests/test_discovery_oracle.py</code> (+6 pins: joint nodes/plan, the corner leads, joint-free byte-identity, the anchor + BN rescues), <code>test_lawdata</code> (kind table), <code>test_guard_sweep</code>, <code>test_conv_fold_rules</code>, <code>test_batch_norm_expand</code>, <code>test_discovery_{gauntlet,evidence,pipeline, autocond,synthesis,enumerate}</code> — all green (the <code>test_every_conditional_ rule_is_swept</code> 125≠124 failure is pre-existing at <code>bb6a2c4</code>). ruff check/format + <code>ty</code> clean on touched files.</p>`,19)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};